WEBVTT

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.250
Spend a lifetime in a gym to get here.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:23.230
Dissing.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:24.780
Honing skills.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.940
All to get to basketball's ultimate stage.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.150
The place where the stakes are highest.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.840
Place where greatness is authenticated.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.390
That place is the NBA Finals.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:57.100
The Chicago Bulls are already a huge part of this league's history.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.940
NBA titles this decade

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.880
and reaching deep for

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:13.480
one more run. Chicago Bulls

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.020
are kings of the NBA

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.720
but someday someone

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:29.860
will dethrone them. Utah Jazz

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.600
came close last year, battling through six tough games.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.580
This year they're back, rested, ready, and with home court advantage.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:47.390
Determined to end the Bulls' run here and write their own chapter in NBA Finals history.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:59.930
Wait is over. The NBA Finals are here. Game 1, next.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:15.920
The NBA on NBC.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.450
The 1998 NBA Finals.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.000
Nice.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.250
It's game one.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.960
The Chicago Bulls versus the Utah Jazz.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.400
The Delta Center in Salt Lake City, one of the loudest buildings in all of sports.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.580
A place where the Jazz enjoy a distinct home court advantage

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.480
and where a sellout crowd is ready to rock the Raptors for game one

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.880
of this rematch in the NBA Finals.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.480
Good news for Jazz fans.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.020
In the past quarter century, prior to this one,

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.860
there have been five rematches in the NBA Finals.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.500
In every instance, the team that lost the first time came back to win the second.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.390
And welcome to Game 1, everybody.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.470
I'm Bob Costas.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.570
We start with this news.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.510
The Chicago Bulls tell us that Dennis Rodman suffered torn ligaments,

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.750
or at least strained ligaments, in his right thumb late in Game 7

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.790
of the Eastern Conference Finals against the Pacers.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.890
He had been expected to start Game 1 of this series.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:18.670
He will not.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:19.510
He is available.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.270
He will play.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.810
Tony Kukoc will start.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.930
We'll have to keep an eye on Dennis, check his minutes,

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.730
see how effective he is in this all-important matchup.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.770
They're looking to him to slow Karl Malone at least a little bit.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.600
Jim Gray will talk with Rodman during our next segment.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:38.030
Now, there is a widespread feeling that of the six times the Chicago Bulls have been to the NBA Finals,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.560
this year's Utah Jazz are the team best equipped to derail them.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.410
They are not awed by the Bulls.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.110
They are rested.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.140
They are ready.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.420
And they believe that this time around they can do it.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.940
This Utah Jazz team includes two of the all-time greats,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.120
certain first ballot Hall of Famers, John Stockton and Karl Malone.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.360
They have played together for 13 years.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.960
No teammates have ever played.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.300
played on the same team so long, whether they were scrubs, Hall of Famers, or anywhere in

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:10.520
between, without winning at least one NBA title. And coming close a year ago was small solace.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:17.130
Yes, we were disappointed. We were excited about getting there and excited about having

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:21.030
the opportunity because of the closeness of it, but we did lose it, so you can't find

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.310
much satisfaction in that.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:27.980
If you're writing a storybook ending, you want to have an opportunity to play the team

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.520
that beat you last year and won the title.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:36.360
And in this business, sometimes you get your wishes, sometimes you don't.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:40.620
We was able to get our wish, and we're looking forward to it.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:46.050
So, too, are basketball fans everywhere, including Isaiah Thomas and Doug Collins.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.770
Well, Zeke, the more things change, the more they remain the same.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.850
For the Utah Jazz, here's the question.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.960
What do you do with Michael?

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.770
Well, Michael Jordan poses so many problems for the defense.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.680
When you're guarding him with a smaller player, such as Jeff Hornacek,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.020
He can just turn around and elevate and shoot right over you.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.430
Then Chicago will come back with the big three, Pippen, Kukoc, and Jordan.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:12.330
Now, you can't leave Jordan, so when they double-team Pippen in the low post, Kukoc is

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.470
there for the long three.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.640
So you say, okay, we'll come double-team you with sides.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:18.080
We'll bring Karl Malone.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.500
But you see Dennis Rodman on offensive glass, and a weak-side offensive player, Tony Kukoc,

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.100
comes up with offensive rebound.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.960
Then last year in the finals, they came from the top, and they left Steve Kerr open for

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.220
What a wide-open day.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:37.920
Now, Michael Jordan has torched Utah this season, averaging close to 35 points a night.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:43.420
And when you double-team him, he frees up on offensive plans for at least 20 shots.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.820
Now, what do you do with Michael Jordan?

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.220
That's the question that the league has been trying to figure out for a very long time.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:50.960
Bob?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.400
And maybe the answer is let him get his the way they did with Shaq in the Western Conference

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.800
Finals as they swept L.A.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.900
Shaq got off, but nobody else did, and they won in force.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.020
straight. I'll tell you one thing, though, guys. Every high school coach in America has to love

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:09.860
this series because these are late 90s teams who play such great fundamental basketball. They play

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:14.680
team ball. They move it around, and there is nothing more basic and yet nothing executed any

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:19.410
closer to perfection than the Utah Jazz pick and roll. Bob, the beauty of the screen roll is that

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:24.370
you take what the defense gives you, and Utah does it better than anybody in the league. You're

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.350
going to see this time Michael Jordan at the top chooses not to rotate, so Stockton's going to

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.890
drive the baseline he gets the double

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.760
team and finds Carl Malone sliding to the open area and he hits the open shot. So Chicago makes

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:39.580
an adjustment. They say we're going to rotate to Carl Malone and we're going to take the shot away

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:45.340
from him. So Malone this time becomes the passer. Stockton to Malone over to Hornacek and he gets

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:51.800
the open shot. Chicago says we'll try it another way. We'll run longly and stay with Malone out

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:58.000
on the perimeter. So Stockton reads it. He drives baseline. Now Hornacek is open in the corner for

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.960
the three-point shot. Regardless of what

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.680
they do they react and they get great shots but the centerpiece of their offense is Carl Malone

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:10.800
when he throws up big numbers you see in the wins 28.5 points they win when he doesn't they lose

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.520
he needs to have big numbers if they're going to find a way to win this championship Bob

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:19.550
in last year's final against the Bulls these were his numbers 24 points around 10 rebounds not bad

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:24.690
shot 44 percent but he didn't come through in some crucial moments and ultimately he graded his

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:29.290
own performance as a C plus how close were the Jazz a year ago as they lost four games to two

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:29.890
Well, except

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.400
Except for game two when they lost by a big margin in Chicago.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:38.060
In their other three defeats, they actually led 129 of the 144 minutes.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.760
And as you look at the overall numbers in the series, there's very little to choose.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.120
The Bulls were simply able to make more big plays in more of the big moments.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.040
And that's why they claim their fifth NBA title.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:53.240
The Jazz think they can make the little adjustments and the big plays down the stretch

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.140
that will change the outcome this time.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.320
We'll be back and we'll be joined by Bill Walton and Hannah Storm

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.840
when we continue from the Delta

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:12.030
center in salt lake city after this game one of the 1998 nba finals welcome back to salt lake

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:16.810
city hannah storm joined by bill walton who will be with us throughout the nba finals peter vesey

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:21.850
and john sally will be joining us at halftime as bob costas mentioned earlier the big news here at

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:26.610
the delta center is the questionable health of dennis rodman he suffered an injury to his right

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.910
thumb sunday night in game seven against indiana and their

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.660
is believed to be some ligament damage. Further tests, however, will be necessary to determine

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:40.180
the extent of Rodman's injury. He will not start tonight, but is expected to play. Tony

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:45.580
Kukoc will start in Rodman's place. A short while ago, Jim Gray spoke with the NBA's leading

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:49.550
rebounder. Dennis, you jammed your thumb in Game 7. You've been wearing a wrap around

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:54.120
it. How will it affect your play tonight? I'm not going to be able to rebound like I

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.700
want to tonight. So, nothing I can do about it is just play basketball. I'm not going to

00:08:58.700 --> 00:08:59.040
everyone

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.920
and tilt the ball and even take a shot in there.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.280
That's just so really freeing.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.220
So I just got to go out there and play as the finals

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.040
or all the injuries to the side.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.980
Does it really affect your game?

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.500
Because the rebounding is so critical and you're not a shooter.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.880
Will it affect your game that much?

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:17.840
Absolutely.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.100
I got to grab the ball in my right hand.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.440
I'm known to grab the ball.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.180
I'm comfortable in my right hand.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.340
I can't grip the ball more or less.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.560
Try to grab it.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.800
Is it going to limit your minutes?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.640
Probably most likely will.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.210
If I'm going good, I'm just going to tell the coach to keep me and I'm ready to play.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:35.910
If I'm not going good, I'm going to sit me down.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.830
I'm not going to contribute to the team, so I'm going to just sit down and cheer for the team.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:40.950
How long until it heals?

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:42.630
I said maybe a week.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:46.430
A week from tonight, Bill, if it takes until then to heal,

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:49.950
and it is expected to be heavily bandaged tonight, would be game four in Chicago.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:54.810
In the meantime, though, Rodman was supposed to see some significant minutes guarding Carl Malone.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.950
So what does this do to the Bulls' defensive strategy?

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.970
Hannah, I just spoke with Bill Jackson, and he is...

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.490
concern. Now, he was planning on starting

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.390
Luke Longley anyway to save Dennis

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:06.090
Rodman for foul trouble

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.190
in the fourth quarter. Bill Wennington,

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.330
Dickie Simpkins, they'll get plenty of time, but

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.390
they're not really the type of players at this

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.270
level. I think there will be critical

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.370
moments in this series when Scottie Pippen, of

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:18.330
all people, will come out and be matched up

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.450
against the great Karl Malone, and that

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.330
will be quite an interesting matchup,

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.130
Hannah. Well, Pippen has had a tremendous

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.330
playoffs from a defensive standpoint, even though he

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.330
struggled somewhat offensively, but he gives up

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:29.970
some to Malone. A couple of...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.360
and almost 30 pounds.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.480
And Scottie Pippen's one of the greatest defensive players of all time.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.800
And Carl Malone's game is no longer about power.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.140
It's no longer about driving to the hoop.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.920
It's all about the passing, the perimeter jumpers,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.220
and it's about that leadership down low.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.820
I really think, Scottie, with his length, with his position,

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.200
with his fundamentals, with great perimeter pressure by Chicago,

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.800
that can be a huge factor for Chicago, Scottie Pippen on Carl Malone.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.400
Well, the Bulls have got to be thinking about a couple of guys

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.700
maybe they could use who were on their playoff roster last year in the finals.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:10:59.900
of

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:03.660
Big body in Jason Caffey, but a man that they traded in February,

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.680
much to the dismay of the rest of his teammates.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.620
And also Brian Williams was a factor not only on the boards,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.380
but did a great job defending Carl Malone last year.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.820
Utah was very competitive, but they lost in six games to the Bulls.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.460
What do they need to do differently this time?

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.960
Hannah, the strategies for beating the Bulls are always the same.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:24.300
The problems for Chicago's opponents are that they're never able to accomplish their goals.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:28.020
Primarily, Utah must establish a dominant low post offense,

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:29.820
and that burden falls squarely.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:37.860
Last year in the finals, Carl Malone normally a go to the basket, get to the free throw line type of player, settled for the perimeter jumper.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.680
Dennis Robin did a terrific job forcing Carl into bad footwork.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.940
Carl Malone flailing away from the outside, not getting those jumpers to fall.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.420
Carl shot just 44%. He's a career 53% shooter.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:52.990
This year, though, he's shooting 79% in the playoffs.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:59.970
Secondly, the Jazz must control their defensive backboard, and this control is a direct result of Utah's perimeter.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:06.580
defense when Michael Jordan takes the shorter Utah guards into the post people can't stand

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:11.780
around and watch they gotta box out they can't let Kukoc and Rodman and Longley get their game

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:17.180
off and then Scottie Pippen loves to launch threes which seemingly turn into passes to players like

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:22.880
Tony Kukoc the defensive the offensive rebounding edge in the finals against the Pacers from the

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:28.700
Eastern Conference that was the difference in that series now this Utah team is vastly improved

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.980
from last year's finalists.

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:33.130
Better skills, better rotations, and much more confident.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:37.870
This Utah team is also the best team the Bulls have ever faced in the finals.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.710
Whether any of this means anything, though,

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:43.270
ultimately comes down to Carl Malone's ability to compete

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:47.130
at the mental level where Michael Jordan has previously reigned supreme.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.830
Will Carl be able to control the flow and the tempo?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.280
Will Carl be able to seize the key pivotal moments

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:55.720
and match the energy burst of Michael Jordan?

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:59.980
Eventually, to win, Carl Malone is going to have to confront Michael Jordan

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.280
greatness head-on and say, Michael, what you have is now mine.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:09.620
It is the two best teams in the NBA battling it out for this year's title.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:13.670
Both the Bulls and the Jazz, 62-20 in the regular season.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.890
Chicago, 11-4 in the playoffs.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.570
Utah, 11-3.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:22.950
After nearly 100 games, these two teams are separated by just one loss.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:27.290
The finals begin here because Utah won both regular season match-ups over Chicago.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.630
The Bulls have beaten every team in the league this season.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.500
except the Utah Jazz.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:35.400
We're closing in on the tip-off of NBA Finals.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:40.640
We'll send it back to Bob Costas, Doug and Isaiah Thomas for the call after these messages.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:53.500
The new Nissan Altima.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.690
Nissan. Life is a journey. Enjoy the ride.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:11.330
loud can it be at the Delta Center? Well, it's not even approaching the top decibels yet with

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:17.070
the game not yet underway, but in preparation for how loud it ultimately will be, Phil Jackson just

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:24.220
walked out onto the floor wearing earplugs. Bob Costas back along with Doug Collins and Isaiah

